insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('41f9aabd-60fc-4e1d-d299-bbcd73b523fe','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af01','What Is Artificial Intelligence?','lesson','Understand the concept
An AI system uses a model to perform a task such as classifying an input or generating a response. A fixed rule follows an explicitly written condition; a learned model derives patterns from examples. Neither arrangement guarantees a correct decision. Start with the task, the available evidence and the cost of an error before deciding whether AI is useful.

Apply it to a concrete case
A campus room booking limit can be enforced by a fixed capacity rule. Classifying free-text maintenance requests may benefit from a trained model, but uncertain cases still need a person. Choose the rule for capacity because its decision criterion is explicit.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Every automated process is AI, and using AI necessarily improves it. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('1d2f9d41-cbd2-5c27-bfd4-4638789246c6','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af02','How Machine Learning Works','lesson','Understand the concept
Machine learning fits a model using examples and an objective. Training performance measures fit to those examples, not performance on unseen cases. Keep evaluation examples separate so you can detect memorization and overfitting. Check whether the evaluation population resembles the population where the model will operate; a good score on an unsuitable sample is weak evidence.

Apply it to a concrete case
A request classifier learns from 80 labeled messages and is evaluated on 20 unused messages. If duplicate messages occur in both sets, the result exaggerates generalization. Remove duplicates before splitting and report the split method.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Perfect training accuracy proves the model will work on new inputs. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('93ddc6ff-ba2a-9358-578c-2ce7a9818433','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af03','Generative AI','lesson','Understand the concept
Generative models produce new text, images or other outputs from learned patterns and supplied context. A plausible output is not a retrieved fact or a guarantee of originality. Use generation to propose drafts, then verify factual claims, permissions and task constraints. Record what the tool contributed so another person can understand how the final artifact was produced.

Apply it to a concrete case
An assistant drafts an event announcement that invents a venue. Compare each factual detail with the approved event brief, remove the invented venue and request the missing information. Stylistic fluency does not resolve the gap.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A fluent generated answer is automatically factual. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('acf42133-afe7-5126-85e2-408a7287e295','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af04','Large Language Models','lesson','Understand the concept
A language model estimates possible continuations from its context and learned parameters. Repeated generation may produce different wording or conclusions. Instruction following and apparent reasoning can be useful, but neither establishes that a factual claim is supported. Evaluate the answer against the task and evidence rather than attributing human understanding or certainty to the model.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two runs give different dates for the same fictional application deadline. The correct action is to consult the official notice, not vote between the outputs. Both continuations can sound equally confident.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: The most confident continuation must be the correct one. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('fb45743c-ccc4-87b1-8bf4-a6ae9388d139','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af05','Tokens, Context & Model Behavior','lesson','Understand the concept
Models process units called tokens, which need not correspond to whole words. The context contains instructions, input and prior conversation within a finite budget. Information outside that context may be unavailable to the model. Put critical constraints where they can be retained, summarize carefully and check that summaries preserve decision-relevant details. A longer prompt can still contain conflicting instructions.

Apply it to a concrete case
A long meeting summary omits that a budget is provisional. The next request treats it as approved. Restore the approval status explicitly and verify the revised output preserves it.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Anything mentioned earlier is permanently available to the model. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b1346c42-46e3-c839-6d6a-609a847ad3e1','c788db68-7431-df85-71b6-3cbd96292338','curriculum-v1-af06','Training, Inference & Fine-Tuning','lesson','Understand the concept
Training adjusts model parameters; inference uses parameters to produce an output. Fine-tuning continues training on a selected dataset to alter behavior. Supplying a document in context does not itself fine-tune the model. For changing factual material, retrieval may be more appropriate than changing parameters. Any approach needs evaluation, access controls and a plan for incorrect outputs.

Apply it to a concrete case
University deadlines change each term. Retrieve the current approved notice instead of fine-tuning solely to memorize dates. Fine-tuning might address a consistent formatting task, but it does not remove the need to check dates.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Uploading a document into a conversation necessarily retrains the model. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('1aa7764a-d168-17f9-ff33-7a4aff2bb0b2','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af07','AI Models & Model Selection','lesson','Understand the concept
Model selection is a decision about fitness for a task. Define representative inputs and observable quality criteria before comparing candidates. Include privacy, latency, cost, accessibility and failure recovery alongside answer quality. Run the same cases under comparable conditions and record versions when known. A small evaluation supports a bounded conclusion, not a universal ranking.

Apply it to a concrete case
For summarizing public notices, one tool is faster but omits eligibility conditions. A rubric that requires accurate eligibility should reject those outputs even if users prefer their style. Report both latency and failed conditions.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: The largest or most popular model is always the best choice. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('c902c1b8-5f6a-f403-43a2-1173a6f17092','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af08','Multimodal AI','lesson','Understand the concept
Multimodal systems accept or generate more than one media type. Images can contain unreadable text, ambiguous scales or cropped context; audio can contain uncertain names or overlapping speakers. Keep the source available, identify uncertain observations and verify consequential details. A generated description is an interpretation, not a replacement for inspecting the original.

Apply it to a concrete case
A chart image has a cropped vertical axis. A model describes a large improvement, but the missing scale prevents judging its size. Obtain the full chart before reporting the magnitude.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An image description is as reliable as directly measured data. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('4f3de54a-d6ed-97ba-fec3-b762e85d472b','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af09','RAG & Knowledge Grounding','lesson','Understand the concept
Retrieval-augmented generation selects source material and supplies it to a model. Retrieval can improve access to relevant information, but irrelevant, stale or malicious material can still enter the context. Apply access controls before retrieval, preserve source references and verify that each claim follows from a source. If no supporting passage exists, report the gap rather than invent an answer.

Apply it to a concrete case
A search finds an expired scholarship notice above the current notice. Filter by the applicable period, cite the current eligibility passage and mark any unanswered question. Retrieval rank alone does not determine authority.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Adding retrieval guarantees that every generated claim is grounded. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('271ea584-f98f-a7c3-2423-4c6e516164c8','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af10','AI Limitations & Hallucinations','lesson','Understand the concept
Models may generate nonexistent citations, stale facts and confident explanations that do not follow from evidence. Repetition across tools is not necessarily independent confirmation. Break an answer into checkable claims, seek primary evidence and record supported, contradicted or unknown status. Communicate uncertainty in terms of what action should wait for verification.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two assistants cite an article that cannot be located. Treat the citation as unverified, search the claimed publisher and remove the unsupported assertion if no source is found. Agreement between assistants does not rescue it.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Agreement between AI tools is sufficient independent verification. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b501dec2-35b4-1605-01af-2fc8ab883107','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af11','Responsible AI','lesson','Understand the concept
Responsible use requires considering who supplies data, who is affected and who can correct a mistake. Minimize personal information, follow applicable institutional rules and disclose assistance accurately. Check whether inputs exclude relevant groups and whether outputs reproduce stereotypes. Give a named person responsibility for consequential decisions and preserve a route to question or revise the outcome.

Apply it to a concrete case
A study-group recommender uses names and grades uploaded without permission. Replace practice data with fictional records, remove unnecessary fields and require authorized review before any real deployment.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Removing names alone eliminates every privacy and fairness risk. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,11) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('7921944d-008e-c855-cac1-6421db71b325','74011f72-9944-9ba1-5d10-ae894a6de440','curriculum-v1-af12','AI Foundations Applied Project','lab','Understand the concept
A defensible AI proposal starts with a user problem, considers a non-AI alternative and defines how success will be measured. Document the input data, proposed model role, verification process and failure handling. Separate results you actually observed from expected results. A reviewer should be able to trace every claimed capability to an artifact or test, not just a demonstration script.

Apply it to a concrete case
For a notice assistant, use public fictional notices, compare summaries with exact source passages and record failures on ambiguous dates. Keep publication behind human approval. This demonstrates bounded assistance rather than autonomous factual authority.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A polished demo proves a solution is reliable in all circumstances. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,12) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('76b4c58c-6976-aa9b-d715-acd97af36de5','c270c2fa-4401-b7e4-09df-ff776152bdd9','curriculum-v1-ap01','AI as a Productivity Tool','lesson','Understand the concept
Productivity means completing useful work to an acceptable standard, not simply generating more output. Measure the time and effort of the current task, including checking and correcting results. Identify a bounded part that AI can assist and retain responsibility for final quality. Compare the full assisted workflow with the original before claiming a benefit.

Apply it to a concrete case
Drafting an email takes two minutes with AI but checking invented details takes eight. The ten-minute total is slower than a five-minute manual draft. Include verification time in the comparison.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Faster generation always means higher productivity. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('4f5de8e1-4803-8947-719a-fe5f2c12f29e','c270c2fa-4401-b7e4-09df-ff776152bdd9','curriculum-v1-ap02','Research With AI','lesson','Understand the concept
Use an assistant to refine a question, suggest search terms and organize supplied material. Treat suggested citations as leads until located and inspected. Prefer primary sources for factual claims, note dates and methods and distinguish evidence from interpretation. Retain a source log so the final conclusion can be checked without trusting the assistant.

Apply it to a concrete case
A summary says a workshop increased employment. The cited survey only measures participant satisfaction. Keep the satisfaction finding and reject the employment claim because the measured outcome differs.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A citation attached to a sentence proves the source supports it. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b971d675-1faf-8c87-c72e-a232ad6cc9a0','c270c2fa-4401-b7e4-09df-ff776152bdd9','curriculum-v1-ap03','AI for Writing & Communication','lesson','Understand the concept
Before drafting, state the audience, purpose, facts that cannot change and desired action. Ask for structure and clarity, then compare the revision with the original facts. Tone improvements can accidentally remove conditions or strengthen uncertain claims. Read the final message as the recipient and verify that its requested action, deadline and contact are unambiguous.

Apply it to a concrete case
An assistant changes a provisional event date into a confirmed date. Restore the provisional status and tell recipients when confirmation will arrive. A smoother sentence is not worth a false promise.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Editing style cannot change the meaning of a message. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('fb52b40a-8c67-57ef-30d2-79b45bd10174','c270c2fa-4401-b7e4-09df-ff776152bdd9','curriculum-v1-ap04','AI for Learning','lesson','Understand the concept
Effective practice asks you to retrieve, explain and apply ideas before seeing an answer. Ask a tutor for questions or hints, attempt them yourself and compare your reasoning with approved material. Keep track of errors and revisit the relevant concept. Follow course rules and do not ask an assistant to supply protected assessment answers or present its work as your own.

Apply it to a concrete case
Instead of requesting the answer to a graded question, explain your current approach and ask for a conceptual hint. After solving an ungraded example, describe why the method works without looking at the solution.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Reading a generated explanation is equivalent to demonstrating understanding. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('55da2940-9ab9-0ba9-756a-3b9013500bf8','c270c2fa-4401-b7e4-09df-ff776152bdd9','curriculum-v1-ap05','AI for Documents & Knowledge Work','lesson','Understand the concept
Document work often combines extraction, interpretation and synthesis. Keep those stages separate: record the exact relevant passage, explain its meaning and then combine it with other evidence. Preserve qualifiers and unresolved contradictions. Use only documents you are authorized to process and maintain references so readers can inspect the original context.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two policy drafts specify different submission dates. A summary should identify the conflict and request the approved version instead of choosing a date silently. Draft status is part of the evidence.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A summary should hide contradictions to make the document easier to read. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('1cb3d587-d905-c066-7a67-10b7b5bb163b','2028fb42-e91b-6cd1-7113-0710cf834ebf','curriculum-v1-ap06','AI for Data/Productivity Tasks','lesson','Understand the concept
An assistant can propose formulas, transformations and table structures, but the output must match the meaning of the data. Specify column names, units and missing-value behavior. Test a small normal case and boundary cases by hand. Preserve raw data and log transformations so a mistaken formula can be corrected without losing the original records.

Apply it to a concrete case
A completion-rate formula divides completed tasks by all rows, including blank placeholders. Count actual assigned tasks instead and verify the result using a three-task example with two completions.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A formula that runs without an error must calculate the intended metric. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('ec8a3936-6a5d-6147-f9bf-2fc95b320149','2028fb42-e91b-6cd1-7113-0710cf834ebf','curriculum-v1-ap07','AI for Meetings & Collaboration','lesson','Understand the concept
Meeting notes should distinguish decisions, proposals, unresolved questions and assigned actions. Obtain appropriate permission for recording or processing discussion. Verify names, owners and deadlines with participants before treating them as commitments. Avoid including unnecessary sensitive detail and retain a correction route when a transcript or summary is wrong.

Apply it to a concrete case
A transcript says Ada could investigate a venue, but the summary assigns her a confirmed booking deadline. Mark the investigation as proposed and request confirmation of ownership and date.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A suggested action in a discussion is already an agreed commitment. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('87a59496-26bf-38bc-f815-9e430c46a081','2028fb42-e91b-6cd1-7113-0710cf834ebf','curriculum-v1-ap08','Building Personal AI Workflows','lesson','Understand the concept
A workflow specifies inputs, transformations, checks and authorized outputs. Define what starts it, how duplicate requests are handled and when a human must approve an action. Store enough context to resume after a failure without repeating an external effect. A manual fallback keeps the underlying task possible when the AI service is unavailable.

Apply it to a concrete case
For weekly planning, collect confirmed deadlines, draft a schedule, check total hours and approve the plan. If generation fails, use the same deadline list with a manual planning template.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A workflow is complete once the AI tool returns a response. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5b9a5d3f-bcfd-51d9-5dee-6426fb3473a6','2028fb42-e91b-6cd1-7113-0710cf834ebf','curriculum-v1-ap09','Verification & Responsible AI Use','lesson','Understand the concept
Verification should match the consequences of an error. Check factual claims, arithmetic, permissions and sensitive data before sharing a result. Record unresolved issues and who can approve the next action. Use synthetic practice data when real data is unnecessary. Do not claim verification merely because a tool returned successfully or the output looks professional.

Apply it to a concrete case
A generated reimbursement summary contains a wrong total and a personal phone number. Recalculate the total, remove the unnecessary number and ask the owner to review before distribution.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A professional-looking output can skip substantive review. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5f727888-708b-01d8-bf0c-ed172d2014ec','2028fb42-e91b-6cd1-7113-0710cf834ebf','curriculum-v1-ap10','AI Productivity Applied Project','lab','Understand the concept
A productivity project needs a baseline, a bounded assisted task and evidence of the result. Include verification effort in time measurements and document failures as well as successes. Show how the workflow handles missing inputs, a service outage and a rejected draft. Clearly label simulated measurements and avoid extrapolating beyond the cases actually evaluated.

Apply it to a concrete case
An event-summary workflow is tested on three briefs. One has no location, so the workflow requests clarification instead of publishing. Report that safe stop alongside successful summaries and total review time.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Only successful examples belong in a project evaluation. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('43feab89-1f98-4a6e-f6c7-44fed9dfe3b0','39bc97bd-445b-141b-e943-d63b4f04b6c5','curriculum-v1-pc01','Prompt Engineering Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
A useful prompt states a goal, relevant input and an observable standard for success. Identify the intended audience and output form without burying the task in unnecessary text. A prompt is a specification for a proposed answer, not a guarantee. Evaluate the result against the specification and revise the instruction when a failure reveals ambiguity.

Apply it to a concrete case
Make a study plan is underspecified. Request a five-hour plan covering three named topics, with session durations that sum to five hours. Check both coverage and arithmetic.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Longer prompts are inherently better prompts. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('97538090-a4f5-35a4-8e8b-603e95aff545','39bc97bd-445b-141b-e943-d63b4f04b6c5','curriculum-v1-pc02','Instructions, Context & Constraints','lesson','Understand the concept
Instructions tell the model what to do; context supplies material needed to do it; constraints define boundaries. Make hard limits explicit and distinguish them from preferences. If the context conflicts with the instruction, require clarification instead of a silent choice. Keep private or irrelevant material out of the prompt.

Apply it to a concrete case
A brief allows only public sources but includes private student notes. Exclude the notes, retain the public-source constraint and explain that the private material is not authorized input.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Providing a piece of context automatically authorizes every use of it. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('ca84ebe7-50b6-6cac-09e3-edf91ea9c6a5','39bc97bd-445b-141b-e943-d63b4f04b6c5','curriculum-v1-pc03','Role, Goal & Output Design','lesson','Understand the concept
A role can guide tone or perspective, but it does not make an answer professionally qualified. State the actual goal and the fields the output must contain. Define how uncertainty and missing information should be represented. Check that each field contains supported information rather than rewarding the appearance of a complete form.

Apply it to a concrete case
Act as an expert does not establish a scholarship deadline. Require a source, date and unresolved-status field. Leave the deadline unresolved when no approved notice supplies it.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Assigning an expert role makes the response authoritative. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('94ec56a3-1e2e-8b7c-1a3d-226f79b770e4','39bc97bd-445b-141b-e943-d63b4f04b6c5','curriculum-v1-pc04','Examples & Few-Shot Prompting','lesson','Understand the concept
Examples can show a desired pattern more clearly than abstract instructions. Include diverse normal cases and at least one boundary case so the pattern does not imply an accidental rule. Separate the example from new input. Evaluate on cases not shown in the prompt to check whether the instruction generalizes beyond copying.

Apply it to a concrete case
A classifier sees only urgent examples containing an exclamation mark. Add an urgent message without punctuation and a non-urgent message with it. Test on a new message to expose the shortcut.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: More examples help even when they all repeat the same accidental pattern. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('23f80c97-792b-fa44-02d5-4473a5be52ea','39bc97bd-445b-141b-e943-d63b4f04b6c5','curriculum-v1-pc05','Structured Outputs','lesson','Understand the concept
Structured output makes fields easier to parse, but valid syntax does not guarantee correct content. Specify required fields, types and allowed values, then validate relationships between fields. Reject or repair invalid output through a bounded process. Keep the original response and validation errors so the failure can be diagnosed.

Apply it to a concrete case
A JSON event record is syntactically valid but its end time precedes its start time. A schema type check alone misses this; add a semantic ordering rule and reject the record.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Valid JSON proves that the represented information is valid. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5adb3ed2-cc2c-8fe4-d5f4-373e9d61c679','ff9b9099-fa44-68f1-ea91-652e69909580','curriculum-v1-pc06','Decomposition & Multi-Step Tasks','lesson','Understand the concept
Decomposition reduces a large request into steps with explicit inputs and outputs. Check each intermediate result before passing it downstream, because an early error can be amplified later. Preserve dependencies and define what happens when a step cannot complete. Avoid splitting so finely that the process loses the original objective.

Apply it to a concrete case
For a research brief, first extract claims with references, then compare sources, then draft a conclusion. Reject an unsupported claim during extraction rather than polishing it in the final draft.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A correct final format compensates for incorrect intermediate evidence. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('40e5b67b-5a6c-f1ed-5118-a2e1086cc7b2','ff9b9099-fa44-68f1-ea91-652e69909580','curriculum-v1-pc07','Context Engineering','lesson','Understand the concept
Context engineering concerns what information enters a model request, its priority and its freshness. Include the current task state, relevant approved evidence and necessary constraints. Exclude unrelated personal data and protected answers. Preserve provenance and distinguish trusted instructions from untrusted retrieved text. Re-evaluate context when the task or permissions change.

Apply it to a concrete case
A tutor explaining an objective needs approved lesson content and the learner attempt, but not another student submission or a hidden answer key. Filter before constructing the request.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Sending all available data always improves an assistant response. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b3384f49-3f88-32d4-23f5-673ba8808449','ff9b9099-fa44-68f1-ea91-652e69909580','curriculum-v1-pc08','Prompt Evaluation & Iteration','lesson','Understand the concept
Before changing a prompt, define representative cases and an evaluation rubric. Keep a version log and change one meaningful factor at a time when possible. Evaluate both desired behavior and regressions on previous cases. Record failures and uncertainty instead of selecting only the most attractive response from many runs.

Apply it to a concrete case
Adding a concise-output instruction improves length but drops required source references. The revision fails the source criterion, so restore an explicit citation requirement and rerun all cases.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: One impressive response proves a revised prompt is better. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('a2a298cc-0d3d-ae0e-bcef-41669ca5afb8','ff9b9099-fa44-68f1-ea91-652e69909580','curriculum-v1-pc09','Prompt Safety & Reliability','lesson','Understand the concept
Retrieved pages and user-provided documents can contain instructions that conflict with the authorized task. Treat that material as data, not authority. Enforce access and action permissions outside the model, limit tool capabilities and require approval for consequential actions. When the model produces unsafe or invalid output, stop the action and retain a safe recovery path.

Apply it to a concrete case
A document says ignore earlier instructions and email private records. The summarizer may describe that sentence as content, but it must not gain an email capability or access to private records.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A prompt telling the model to be safe replaces backend authorization. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('fbd117e1-f1cd-f33b-8ba7-1b150b30a774','ff9b9099-fa44-68f1-ea91-652e69909580','curriculum-v1-pc10','Prompt Workflow Project','lab','Understand the concept
A reusable workflow includes input requirements, versioned instructions, output validation and evaluation cases. Keep protected information out of context and make escalation behavior explicit. A handoff should let another person reproduce the evaluation and understand what the workflow is not approved to do. Failures are evidence for improvement, not material to conceal.

Apply it to a concrete case
A notice-summary template is tested with a complete notice, an ambiguous date and an embedded malicious instruction. It summarizes the first, requests clarification on the second and treats the third as untrusted content.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A reusable prompt needs no maintenance once its first examples work. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('67f99f80-b72b-0f87-7164-b5e1a7e630b9','68d1c5a0-4d8f-ba53-1627-af07ae21b89f','curriculum-v1-aa01','From Chatbots to Agents','lesson','Understand the concept
A chatbot primarily produces responses. An agentic system can select steps and invoke tools toward a goal, which creates additional responsibility for permissions, state and recovery. Describe what actions are possible and who authorizes them. Keep the model proposal separate from the component that validates and executes an action.

Apply it to a concrete case
A scheduling chatbot suggests a time; an agent with calendar access can create an event. The second system needs participant checks, explicit permission and duplicate prevention before writing.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Giving a chatbot tools makes every action it proposes authorized. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('231c935d-4446-486e-8757-9dde9243314e','68d1c5a0-4d8f-ba53-1627-af07ae21b89f','curriculum-v1-aa02','Agent Goals & Task Planning','lesson','Understand the concept
An agent goal should specify the desired outcome, constraints and conditions for stopping or escalating. Plans break the goal into actions whose results can be checked. Limit time, tool calls and external effects so a failed plan cannot continue indefinitely. Revise a plan using observed results rather than assuming every previous step succeeded.

Apply it to a concrete case
A campus event assistant may find three venue options but cannot book one. It stops after producing verified options or after its search budget is exhausted, then asks an authorized organizer to decide.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An agent should keep trying indefinitely until it reaches its goal. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('02718f6d-54fe-d2ae-ead9-11da0e0ef41c','68d1c5a0-4d8f-ba53-1627-af07ae21b89f','curriculum-v1-aa03','Tools & Function Calling','lesson','Understand the concept
Tool calling represents an action request using a defined name and arguments. The application must validate argument types, permissions and business rules before execution. Treat tool results as fallible input and avoid exposing unnecessary data to the model. An allowlist limits the available actions; it does not replace per-record authorization.

Apply it to a concrete case
A proposed update_task call names another learner task. Although the arguments match the schema, the server rejects it because the caller does not own that record. Syntax validation and authorization answer different questions.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A schema-valid tool call is automatically safe to execute. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('53b05cda-0979-880a-e400-016c87d17b1b','68d1c5a0-4d8f-ba53-1627-af07ae21b89f','curriculum-v1-aa04','Memory, Context & State','lesson','Understand the concept
Conversation context is information presented to a model; durable state records what the system has actually done. Store authoritative status changes in the application database with ownership and audit information. Treat remembered statements as claims unless they correspond to verified records. Define retention and deletion rules for stored context.

Apply it to a concrete case
An assistant says a reminder was sent, but the delivery record is still pending. The workflow reports pending and retries according to policy instead of marking it delivered based on the message.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A statement in conversation is an authoritative record of an action. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('9339f67d-d383-dd4b-0048-48ca87495806','68d1c5a0-4d8f-ba53-1627-af07ae21b89f','curriculum-v1-aa05','APIs for Agents','lesson','Understand the concept
An API exposes a contract for requests and responses. An agent integration should validate inputs, protect credentials and interpret status codes before using the response. Timeouts leave some outcomes uncertain, so check idempotency and remote state before repeating a mutation. Limit accessible endpoints and data to the authorized task.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task-creation request times out after reaching the server. Retry with the same idempotency key or query the prior request result; a blind new request could create two tasks.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A timeout proves the remote action never happened. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('33cd1200-0891-48cf-215d-3be4ad31c583','e277dbdd-1679-1a27-fc00-43f03b68ea0d','curriculum-v1-aa06','Workflow Automation','lesson','Understand the concept
A workflow records the order and conditions under which work proceeds. Make transitions explicit, persist the current state and decide which steps can be retried safely. Keep domain completion authoritative: a workflow should reflect an approved result, not manufacture one. Human decisions remain pending until the authorized person acts.

Apply it to a concrete case
A submission workflow waits for a reviewer decision. Advancing the queue item alone cannot approve the submission; the review record must show the required decision and evidence.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Moving a workflow card to done proves the underlying domain work is complete. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('3559736a-3804-5163-9951-9adb33d8fe44','e277dbdd-1679-1a27-fc00-43f03b68ea0d','curriculum-v1-aa07','Human Approval & Guardrails','lesson','Understand the concept
Approval is permission for a specific proposed action under stated conditions. Show the reviewer the relevant inputs and consequences, record their decision and verify that the proposal has not changed before execution. If it changes materially, request fresh approval. Enforce these rules in the action service, not solely in the interface.

Apply it to a concrete case
An organizer approves a message for 20 recipients. If the agent changes the recipient list to 200, the old approval is insufficient. Bind approval to the reviewed proposal and require another decision.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: One approval authorizes any later variation of the proposed action. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('8e998531-837b-d0f3-44e4-e2a7710ca154','e277dbdd-1679-1a27-fc00-43f03b68ea0d','curriculum-v1-aa08','Agent Reliability & Observability','lesson','Understand the concept
Record step identifiers, attempts, outcomes and safe error details so a run can be reconstructed. Do not log secrets or unnecessary personal data. Use bounded retries for recoverable failures and escalate repeated or permanent failures. Monitor actual outcomes, including duplicate prevention and recovery, rather than counting model responses as completed work.

Apply it to a concrete case
A tool returns a validation error three times with unchanged input. Retrying again will not repair the input. Stop, record the failing field and request correction rather than consuming more attempts.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Every failure is best handled by retrying the same request. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('0dc13f25-d753-53ac-a047-a32a5ac26364','e277dbdd-1679-1a27-fc00-43f03b68ea0d','curriculum-v1-aa09','Multi-Step Agent Systems','lesson','Understand the concept
Multiple agent steps can divide research, drafting and validation, but each needs a clear input/output contract and minimal permissions. Validate handoffs and retain a single authoritative record of completed actions. Independent review requires different evidence or checks, not merely another agent agreeing with the first. Bound cycles and make human escalation possible.

Apply it to a concrete case
A research step supplies source-linked claims to a drafting step. A validator checks those claims against the sources before publication. If a source is missing, the flow returns for research instead of accepting agreement among agents.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Several agents agreeing is equivalent to independent evidence. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('8b28a319-76e5-0bb5-5e5c-2ad724d62328','e277dbdd-1679-1a27-fc00-43f03b68ea0d','curriculum-v1-aa10','Build an Agent Workflow','lab','Understand the concept
An agent project should expose its goal, tools, permissions, state model and verification rules. Demonstrate normal operation and failure recovery with synthetic or authorized inputs. Record tool proposals separately from accepted actions and show that invalid or unauthorized requests cannot create side effects. Document how to stop the system and inspect a failed run.

Apply it to a concrete case
A notice assistant retrieves approved notices, drafts a summary and waits for publication approval. An injected instruction is ignored, a timeout does not duplicate publication and rejection returns the draft for correction.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A successful happy-path run is sufficient certification for an agent. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('c0934ef7-f84b-a5f0-e8cd-05f9b4638f2b','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se01','How Software Works','lesson','Understand the concept
Software executes instructions over data. A user interface collects input, application logic interprets it and storage may preserve the result. Distinguish code, runtime state and persisted data when diagnosing behavior. A screen update does not prove a database write succeeded; verify the result at the boundary responsible for it.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task appears immediately in a list, but the server rejects its save. The UI should show the failure and avoid presenting the task as durably stored. Reloading reveals whether persistence occurred.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: If an item is visible on screen, it must already be stored. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('461413fc-ff76-f4be-f452-ee3b69c2df9a','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se02','Programming Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
Programming translates a problem into operations with defined inputs and outputs. Start with a small example, write the expected result and then express the steps needed to obtain it. Separate the algorithm from a particular language syntax. Test an ordinary case, an empty input and an invalid input before expanding the program.

Apply it to a concrete case
To total study minutes, initialize a total, validate each duration and add valid values. Reject a negative duration rather than silently lowering the total. For 20 and 30 minutes, the result is 50.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Code is correct once its syntax is accepted. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('7dc64e57-2013-4275-189c-a8fdcb5b5251','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se03','Variables, Types & Data','lesson','Understand the concept
Variables name values; types describe which operations and representations are valid. A string containing digits is not automatically a valid numeric measurement. Parse deliberately, validate the allowed range and retain units. Distinguish absent values from meaningful zero values, because treating them as interchangeable can produce misleading results.

Apply it to a concrete case
A form supplies the string 30 for minutes. Convert it to a number and check that it is positive. An empty string is missing input, not evidence of a zero-minute session.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Missing data and zero are interchangeable. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('aafe433d-7bfe-8b07-b644-e5bfc55d3f40','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se04','Logic & Control Flow','lesson','Understand the concept
Conditions choose which instructions run; loops repeat work over a collection or until a condition changes. Make boundaries explicit and ensure loops can terminate. Trace representative values by hand before relying on execution. Pay attention to inclusive versus exclusive comparisons and to what happens when the collection is empty.

Apply it to a concrete case
A reminder is due when its date is today or earlier and it is not completed. Checking only dates before today misses today tasks; ignoring completion sends unnecessary reminders.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Testing one true branch is enough to verify a conditional rule. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('6cd26fd1-450e-df74-c9fd-b4b397b03398','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se05','Functions & Modularity','lesson','Understand the concept
A function packages behavior behind named inputs and an output. Separate pure calculations from effects such as database writes so each can be checked independently. State preconditions and error behavior, and avoid hidden dependencies on unrelated global state. Modularity helps when boundaries reflect responsibilities rather than arbitrary file size.

Apply it to a concrete case
A completion-rate function accepts completed and total counts and returns no rate when total is zero. A separate function formats the result for display. This keeps the mathematical decision independent from UI wording.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A function is reusable even if its required inputs are hidden global variables. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('f3fb6816-f760-8e80-44b5-5d4a99765812','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se06','Data Structures','lesson','Understand the concept
Lists preserve ordered items, maps associate keys with values and sets represent unique values. Select a structure by the operations the program needs rather than by habit. Define how duplicates and missing keys behave. A structure that is convenient in memory does not itself enforce database consistency or user authorization.

Apply it to a concrete case
Use a list for tasks in display order and a set for completed task IDs when checking membership. If task IDs are duplicated, investigate the source instead of hiding inconsistent records through display logic.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Using a set in the UI guarantees the database contains no duplicates. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('e440c23d-bfdc-dab1-8ef9-4dc12fbe736f','55bad234-60bd-7bd6-1a04-c22788f812cb','curriculum-v1-se07','Web Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
A browser requests resources from a server. HTML provides document structure, CSS presentation and JavaScript interactive behavior. URLs identify resources, while HTTP requests and responses carry method, status, headers and optional bodies. Network failures and server errors are normal possibilities, so an interactive page needs visible loading and failure states.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task page loads HTML, then requests task data. If the data request fails, the page should explain the failure rather than display an empty list as if no tasks exist.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An empty screen always means the server returned no records. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('9e8afe20-c6fb-c610-1f6a-d37d3068eeb4','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se08','Frontend Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
Frontend work connects user actions to application behavior. Use semantic controls with labels, keyboard access and clear validation messages. Track loading and failure explicitly, and prevent accidental duplicate submission without trapping the user. Client validation improves feedback, but the server must still validate and authorize the request.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task form labels the title field, reports a missing title and disables repeated submission while saving. On server rejection it preserves the typed title and explains how to retry.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Client-side form validation makes server validation unnecessary. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('ceee1ff6-aa84-1d3c-0420-4bc143955065','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se09','Backend Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
A backend receives untrusted requests, resolves the caller identity and applies authorization and validation before changing state. Use transactions when related writes must succeed together. Return useful errors without exposing secrets. The server cannot rely on a hidden button or a client-supplied owner ID as proof that a mutation is allowed.

Apply it to a concrete case
A learner submits a task update with another learner ID. The server derives the actor from the session and checks record ownership, rejecting the request regardless of the submitted owner field.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A client-supplied user ID is trustworthy proof of identity. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b3fb6239-caf2-e269-d09f-6d0674baa3cd','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se10','Databases','lesson','Understand the concept
A relational database stores records in tables connected by keys. Primary keys identify records; foreign keys preserve relationships; uniqueness and check constraints protect business invariants. Use transactions for related changes and additive migrations to evolve deployed schemas. Keep learner history intact when introducing new fields or versions.

Apply it to a concrete case
An enrollment table references learner and course IDs and has a unique learner/course pair. Two concurrent enrollment requests then cannot create duplicate enrollment records even if both passed an earlier UI check.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Checking for duplicates in the interface is equivalent to a database constraint. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('50edb33e-36d1-2bb5-ea3c-dfc6da22557c','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se11','APIs & REST','lesson','Understand the concept
An API contract states what a caller sends, what the server returns and which failures are possible. Resource-oriented HTTP designs use methods with defined intent, such as reading or creating a resource. Validate payloads, paginate collections and enforce record-level authorization. Do not expose internal errors or assume every response contains the expected shape.

Apply it to a concrete case
POST /tasks accepts a title and returns the created task. A missing title is a validation error; an invalid session is an authentication error. Listing tasks returns only the caller authorized records.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Every non-success response should be treated as an empty successful result. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,11) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b10287a8-eadc-f749-1a87-ad0933d3b1b0','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se12','Git & Version Control','lesson','Understand the concept
Version control records changes so their purpose and history can be inspected. Review the working diff, stage only related files and write a commit message explaining the behavior changed. Branches isolate work; merging combines histories and may require deliberate conflict resolution. Never commit credentials, and verify the final combined behavior after resolving a conflict.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two branches modify task validation. A conflict is not resolved by blindly accepting one side; compare intended rules, combine them where appropriate and run validation tests on the result.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A clean merge proves the combined program behaves correctly. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,12) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('6e887151-ff8e-9e3a-c368-d4bec33d2e50','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se13','Testing, Debugging & Deployment','lesson','Understand the concept
A useful test checks observable behavior and fails when that behavior is wrong. Reproduce a defect, narrow its cause and make the smallest justified correction. Run relevant regression tests before building and deploying. Keep environment configuration separate from code, protect secrets and define rollback and health checks before changing a running service.

Apply it to a concrete case
A date-boundary bug omits tasks due today. Add a failing today-case test, correct the comparison, rerun prior cases and verify the deployed task list with a safe test record.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Passing local tests guarantees deployment cannot fail. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,13) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('80f37c75-3a89-2f4b-2afd-5e02f9bd37f9','2f872221-714c-3946-7369-cd232335be49','curriculum-v1-se14','Software Engineering Project','lab','Understand the concept
A software project joins specification, implementation, data and operations. Define acceptance criteria before building and retain evidence of normal and negative tests. Document setup without embedding secrets, explain access rules and record limitations. A working UI is only part of the result; persistence, authorization and recovery must also be demonstrated.

Apply it to a concrete case
A study-task app lets each learner create and complete their own tasks. Tests cover invalid titles, duplicate requests and cross-user edits. A README explains setup and an observed deployment health check.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A project is complete when the homepage looks finished. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,14) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('e23e2928-3601-7c59-628f-799c3218ca8f','23071e38-a8c3-2f6b-9b53-9a9c7a239921','curriculum-v1-da01','Data Literacy','lesson','Understand the concept
Data analysis begins with a question, not a chart. Define the population, time period, measurement and decision the analysis should support. Distinguish observations from interpretations and note what the dataset does not contain. A precise question helps avoid calculating a convenient metric that does not address the actual problem.

Apply it to a concrete case
How many students completed a project this term differs from what proportion of enrolled students completed. The second question requires an enrollment denominator and a consistent period.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Any available metric is suitable for the decision being made. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('ecd7e758-4c24-69b9-b5d5-a4fe7d262a45','23071e38-a8c3-2f6b-9b53-9a9c7a239921','curriculum-v1-da02','Data Types & Structures','lesson','Understand the concept
Data can represent categories, counts, measurements, dates or text. The representation affects valid comparisons and calculations. Define units and allowed values in a data dictionary, and distinguish an unknown value from zero or an empty category. Consistent structure makes analysis reproducible and reveals incompatible records before aggregation.

Apply it to a concrete case
Study duration recorded as hours in one row and minutes in another cannot be summed safely until units are standardized. Preserve the original values and record the conversion.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Values in the same column necessarily use the same unit. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('4d66ac5f-6481-68e6-b9bb-84cc341cdbce','23071e38-a8c3-2f6b-9b53-9a9c7a239921','curriculum-v1-da03','Data Collection & Quality','lesson','Understand the concept
Collection methods determine whose experiences are represented and how reliably they are measured. Check sampling, coverage, definitions and missing responses. More records do not fix a systematically excluded group. Record how data was obtained and what conclusions the collection method can and cannot support.

Apply it to a concrete case
An online-only survey misses students with unreliable internet. Adding more online responses may improve precision within that group while leaving the coverage gap unchanged.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A large dataset is automatically representative. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('f4d8042f-66d4-457d-49a9-95dc57aa6e7e','23071e38-a8c3-2f6b-9b53-9a9c7a239921','curriculum-v1-da04','Data Cleaning','lesson','Understand the concept
Cleaning addresses duplicates, missing values, invalid ranges and inconsistent categories. Define rules before changing data and retain the raw version. Do not silently replace unknown values with zero or remove inconvenient outliers. Keep a change log explaining what changed, why and how the decision could affect analysis.

Apply it to a concrete case
A negative study duration is invalid, while an unusually long duration may be a real outlier. Flag both for review but do not apply the same automatic deletion rule to them.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Every unusual value is an error that should be deleted. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('1f32bd42-4484-bf30-0897-1195d9850ce1','23071e38-a8c3-2f6b-9b53-9a9c7a239921','curriculum-v1-da05','SQL & Query Thinking','lesson','Understand the concept
A query selects records, relates tables and summarizes values. Identify the grain of each table before joining: one learner may have many submissions, so a join can multiply rows. Decide whether you need counts of rows, distinct learners or another measure. Check the query against a tiny example whose answer you can calculate by hand.

Apply it to a concrete case
Joining learners to submissions yields three rows for a learner with three submissions. Counting rows overstates the number of learners; count distinct learner IDs when that is the question.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Counting joined rows always counts the original entities. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('aad981c5-96c8-0964-ec37-34f12be93f72','43561edf-5cdb-6105-8e44-829ebdb0b87f','curriculum-v1-da06','Exploratory Analysis','lesson','Understand the concept
Exploration checks distributions, missingness, relationships and unusual observations before formal conclusions. Compare groups using consistent definitions and inspect both central tendency and variation. Treat discovered patterns as questions to investigate, especially when many comparisons were tried. Record analysis choices so others can distinguish exploration from a preplanned test.

Apply it to a concrete case
Average study time rises because one student reports an extreme value. Compare the median and distribution, inspect the record and explain how sensitive the mean is to it.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A pattern discovered during exploration is already a proven explanation. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('8a0afce1-e2fe-2594-1ca2-b9ab82d879be','43561edf-5cdb-6105-8e44-829ebdb0b87f','curriculum-v1-da07','Statistics for Decision Making','lesson','Understand the concept
Statistics summarizes variation and uncertainty, but conclusions depend on sampling and assumptions. Report denominators with rates and avoid treating a small difference as decisive without context. Association alone does not identify causation; alternative explanations may remain. State what additional evidence would change the decision.

Apply it to a concrete case
Six of ten students and sixty of one hundred students both give a 60 percent completion rate, but the smaller group provides less stable evidence about a wider population. Report group sizes with the rates.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Equal percentages from very different sample sizes provide identical evidence. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('92e3a477-bef5-05fe-5c7c-1899b6359655','43561edf-5cdb-6105-8e44-829ebdb0b87f','curriculum-v1-da08','Data Visualization','lesson','Understand the concept
A chart encodes data using position, length, color or other visual features. Choose an encoding that matches the question and label units, categories and time periods. Avoid misleading scales and inaccessible color-only distinctions. Include uncertainty or missing-data notes when they affect interpretation, and keep the underlying values available.

Apply it to a concrete case
A bar chart starting its axis near the smallest value exaggerates a small completion-rate difference. Use an appropriate baseline and show the rates and cohort sizes explicitly.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A visually dramatic chart necessarily communicates the data more accurately. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5fcb2d6a-d464-c132-742a-927d6d0d8d99','43561edf-5cdb-6105-8e44-829ebdb0b87f','curriculum-v1-da09','AI-Assisted Analytics','lesson','Understand the concept
AI can suggest queries, formulas and narratives, but it may misunderstand the dataset or invent findings. Supply a data dictionary and a bounded question, then inspect the proposed method. Verify calculations on small cases and trace every narrative claim to an actual result. Do not send sensitive records to an unauthorized service.

Apply it to a concrete case
An assistant describes an increase in monthly revenue from a table containing only transaction counts. Reject the revenue claim because the required price data is absent, even if the query runs.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A successful query makes the generated interpretation trustworthy. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('600a9a20-d303-087f-c9d6-32a6fa318744','43561edf-5cdb-6105-8e44-829ebdb0b87f','curriculum-v1-da10','Data Analytics Project','lab','Understand the concept
A data project should connect a decision question to collection, cleaning, analysis and communication. Keep source provenance and transformation records, validate key calculations and report limitations. If a real dataset cannot be lawfully obtained, mark a synthetic exercise clearly rather than implying real-world findings. A reviewer needs enough material to reproduce the conclusion.

Apply it to a concrete case
A campus transport analysis reports waiting-time distributions from authorized observations, explains missing periods and avoids claiming all students are represented. The cleaned data and calculation steps accompany the chart.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A polished dashboard replaces the need for data provenance and methods. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('a03114b4-72ec-6b82-4aaf-6ecd6ddb8a5e','556bb9db-fef8-b369-47fe-ad4809b6268c','curriculum-v1-cl01','What Is Cloud Computing?','lesson','Understand the concept
Cloud computing provides computing resources through a service rather than requiring the application team to own every machine. Service models divide operational responsibilities differently, but the application owner still needs to manage data, access and configuration. Evaluate the required capability, reliability and cost instead of assuming cloud hosting removes operational work.

Apply it to a concrete case
A managed database may handle machine maintenance while the application team still defines who can read student records. A managed service does not decide the correct access policy for the product.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Moving an application to the cloud transfers all security responsibility to the provider. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('e1a9c543-9bbc-f420-b060-011a1a048500','556bb9db-fef8-b369-47fe-ad4809b6268c','curriculum-v1-cl02','Compute, Storage & Networking','lesson','Understand the concept
Compute executes code, storage persists data and networking connects components. Trace where a request runs and where its data must remain after the process stops. Distinguish temporary local files from durable storage and private connections from public endpoints. Resource choices affect latency, availability, cost and the consequences of a component failure.

Apply it to a concrete case
An uploaded project file saved only on a temporary application filesystem disappears when the instance is replaced. Store it durably and keep an authorized reference in the database.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A file written by a cloud process is necessarily durable. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('70fcf68c-9708-a973-d05a-21adfe9f1781','556bb9db-fef8-b369-47fe-ad4809b6268c','curriculum-v1-cl03','Cloud Databases','lesson','Understand the concept
A cloud database still needs a sound schema, least-privilege access and tested recovery. Separate application credentials from administrative credentials and protect connection configuration. Apply migrations deliberately and verify that old records remain valid. A backup is useful only if the team can restore the required data within an acceptable time.

Apply it to a concrete case
A team has daily backups but has never restored one. Run a restore exercise in an isolated environment, check record counts and relationships and document recovery time before relying on the backup plan.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: The existence of a backup proves recovery will work. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('1fc9b3f8-fe23-f566-b858-db4f98591d32','556bb9db-fef8-b369-47fe-ad4809b6268c','curriculum-v1-cl04','APIs & Cloud Services','lesson','Understand the concept
Cloud services expose APIs with authentication, quotas and failure modes. Keep credentials server-side when they confer privileged access, validate responses and set timeouts. Handle rate limits with bounded retries and avoid repeating non-idempotent actions blindly. Record safe request identifiers so failures can be investigated without logging secrets.

Apply it to a concrete case
An email service rejects a request due to a temporary quota. Queue a bounded retry using the original message identity rather than creating a new message for every attempt.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Retrying with a new request identity is always harmless. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5343683b-feef-96df-38c5-d57db50f060f','c2b3d0a3-e8b3-48f9-b478-e8abad24df4f','curriculum-v1-cl05','Serverless & Modern Deployment','lesson','Understand the concept
Serverless execution runs code on demand under platform-defined limits. Do not assume one process will retain memory, local files or a long-running connection between requests. Persist durable state outside the invocation, make retries safe and account for time limits. Deployment configuration should describe required environment values without containing their secret contents.

Apply it to a concrete case
A function stores processed submission IDs in memory. A new instance loses that set and processes a retry twice. Move deduplication into a database uniqueness rule or durable idempotency record.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: In-memory state survives every serverless invocation. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('e9d2ed9f-45ec-25c5-5cf7-cff9af4b10a4','c2b3d0a3-e8b3-48f9-b478-e8abad24df4f','curriculum-v1-cl06','Identity, Secrets & Configuration','lesson','Understand the concept
Configuration describes how an application connects to its environment. Some values are public identifiers; others grant authority and must remain secret. Store secrets in an approved secret mechanism, restrict access and rotate exposed credentials. Use different identities for development and production where practical, and never treat hiding a value in frontend code as protection.

Apply it to a concrete case
A privileged database key is embedded in a browser bundle. Removing it from the repository alone is insufficient because it may already be exposed; revoke or rotate it and move privileged operations behind authorized server code.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A secret is safe if its variable name is obscure. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('241c42fa-8d78-39ea-7e29-cd312fb57619','c2b3d0a3-e8b3-48f9-b478-e8abad24df4f','curriculum-v1-cl07','Reliability, Scaling & Observability','lesson','Understand the concept
Reliability concerns whether users can complete the intended task, not just whether a process is running. Measure errors, latency and critical workflow outcomes with safe logs and correlation identifiers. Scaling adds capacity but may expose shared-state or database bottlenecks. Define alerts, ownership and recovery procedures that correspond to actual user impact.

Apply it to a concrete case
The homepage returns successfully while task writes fail. A process-only health check stays green; an application health check that verifies the write dependency detects the real outage.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A reachable homepage proves every application workflow is healthy. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('ca54f761-b2b3-f0fd-b9a1-a600de83fc8c','c2b3d0a3-e8b3-48f9-b478-e8abad24df4f','curriculum-v1-cl08','Deploy a Cloud Application','lab','Understand the concept
A deployment project needs a reproducible build, explicit configuration, controlled access and a recovery plan. Verify the running version through a real user journey and inspect operational signals. Record which checks ran and which remain unexecuted. Use a test environment and authorized data before exposing a service to real users.

Apply it to a concrete case
After deploying a task app, create and reload a task, verify cross-user denial and inspect the health signal. If persistence fails, stop release promotion and return to the previous working version.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A successful deployment command proves the application works for users. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('2d0cf978-8ae7-0883-daec-aad1d4d0a16d','49d9cde2-9346-7bc0-e495-765aa8c62874','curriculum-v1-cs01','Cybersecurity Fundamentals','lesson','Understand the concept
Security protects the confidentiality, integrity and availability of systems and data. Identify the asset and the actor or event that could harm it before choosing a control. A vulnerability is a weakness; risk also depends on likelihood and impact. Work only in authorized environments and use fictional data for learning exercises.

Apply it to a concrete case
Student submissions are an asset. An overly broad read policy is a weakness that may expose them to other users. Restricting access and testing denial directly addresses that risk.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Security is only about preventing malicious code execution. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('c9a1829e-b6b9-6560-5f59-88f494bb7234','49d9cde2-9346-7bc0-e495-765aa8c62874','curriculum-v1-cs02','Identity & Authentication','lesson','Understand the concept
Authentication establishes which identity is making a request, using a mechanism such as a credential or an existing session. Protect credentials, validate sessions server-side and handle expiry and revocation. Authentication does not decide which records the person may access. Error handling should avoid exposing unnecessary account information.

Apply it to a concrete case
A user remains on an open page after their session expires. The next save must revalidate the session and ask them to sign in, preserving unsaved work safely rather than trusting the old UI state.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A page that loaded while signed in can trust the user forever. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('fa75fa6f-224d-64b7-d82c-14ce8f2542cf','49d9cde2-9346-7bc0-e495-765aa8c62874','curriculum-v1-cs03','Authorization & Least Privilege','lesson','Understand the concept
Authorization determines whether an authenticated actor may perform a specific action on a specific resource. Grant only the permissions needed and deny by default. Enforce the decision at the backend and database boundary where applicable. Test both allowed and denied cases, including users with the same role in different organizations.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two learners can each edit their own tasks. Changing a task ID in a request must not let one edit the other task, even though both are authenticated learners.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Users with the same role may access all records belonging to that role. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('d78f6d10-e823-5a00-5eb8-a13c707e53ba','49d9cde2-9346-7bc0-e495-765aa8c62874','curriculum-v1-cs04','Data Privacy & Protection','lesson','Understand the concept
Privacy work begins by asking whether a data item is needed at all. State the purpose, who may access it and when it should be deleted or reviewed. Protect data in transit and storage, but recognize that encryption does not justify unnecessary collection. Use applicable institutional policy and qualified guidance for legal requirements.

Apply it to a concrete case
A study planner needs available hours, not a government identity number. Remove the unnecessary field and define a retention period for obsolete schedules rather than keeping every record indefinitely.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Encryption makes every data-collection choice appropriate. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('87073c9c-b93c-1f3d-9dbd-2151b5cf494d','49d9cde2-9346-7bc0-e495-765aa8c62874','curriculum-v1-cs05','Web/Application Security','lesson','Understand the concept
Web applications receive untrusted input in forms, URLs and API requests. Validate expected values, use safe database query mechanisms and encode output for its context. Apply authorization before returning or changing records. Security tests should use a controlled test application and verify that malformed or unauthorized input is rejected without exposing private data.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task title containing markup should be displayed as text rather than executed as page behavior. A user ID in the URL must still be checked against the session authorization.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Input validation alone prevents every web application security issue. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('3e21b66f-8f9e-df47-a548-e5071cb30bd5','5d81bf85-f7af-3372-a48f-2d5eca3015f2','curriculum-v1-cs06','Social Engineering & Human Risk','lesson','Understand the concept
Social engineering manipulates trust, urgency or authority to obtain information or actions. Pause when a request seeks credentials, unusual payments or bypassed procedures. Verify through a known independent channel rather than the contact supplied in the suspicious message. Report the event and preserve useful evidence without spreading sensitive material.

Apply it to a concrete case
A message claiming to be university IT asks for a password through a new link. Use the known IT portal or contact directory to verify the request, and do not submit the password.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An urgent message from a familiar display name is sufficient proof of authority. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('8c727d79-bfa1-1478-0268-57c4881a2068','5d81bf85-f7af-3372-a48f-2d5eca3015f2','curriculum-v1-cs07','AI Security','lesson','Understand the concept
AI systems introduce risks such as malicious instructions in retrieved content, excessive tool authority and leakage through prompts or logs. Treat model output as untrusted until validated. Filter authorized context before calling the model and enforce tool permissions outside it. Test conceptual attacks in a controlled fixture without exposing real secrets.

Apply it to a concrete case
A retrieved note tells the assistant to reveal another learner attempts. The context builder never supplies those attempts, and the tool layer rejects the cross-user request even if proposed.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: The model can be trusted to enforce all access rules from a safety prompt. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('db7c89af-7cde-2b88-ec7b-d1747dd5c7e2','5d81bf85-f7af-3372-a48f-2d5eca3015f2','curriculum-v1-cs08','Responsible AI & Bias','lesson','Understand the concept
Bias can arise from collection, labels, objectives and how outputs are used. Examine whether relevant groups are represented and whether errors have unequal consequences. Avoid treating one aggregate metric as a complete fairness assessment. Include affected people in review where appropriate and provide a process to challenge or correct outcomes.

Apply it to a concrete case
A recommendation system performs well overall but repeatedly excludes students with limited connectivity. Inspect group-specific outcomes and the input assumptions instead of relying solely on the overall score.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A high overall accuracy score proves a system is fair. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5fa4c5e2-4c6d-e775-c303-79f8529c9db3','5d81bf85-f7af-3372-a48f-2d5eca3015f2','curriculum-v1-cs09','Threat/Risk Analysis','lesson','Understand the concept
Threat analysis asks what must be protected, where trust changes and how a failure could occur. Describe a plausible scenario, existing controls and remaining uncertainty. Prioritize by impact and likelihood rather than by how dramatic a threat sounds. Assign owners and define evidence that a mitigation actually works.

Apply it to a concrete case
A public file URL exposes private project evidence. The mitigation is authorized access to the object, not merely removing the link from a page. Test access as another user and anonymously.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Hiding a private resource link is equivalent to restricting access. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('c6af7e5d-af66-3a99-a900-16ebc67bf421','5d81bf85-f7af-3372-a48f-2d5eca3015f2','curriculum-v1-cs10','Security Assessment Project','lab','Understand the concept
A security assessment needs explicit scope and authorization, an asset model and reproducible observations. Use controlled test accounts and avoid destructive or unauthorized actions. Separate confirmed findings from hypotheses, document mitigations and rerun the relevant tests. A report should explain residual risks and what was outside the assessment.

Apply it to a concrete case
Two test learners exercise evidence access. One can read the other private artifact, so the report records the boundary failure, applies an access-policy correction and verifies both allowed and denied reads.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Finding no issue in a limited review proves the whole system is secure. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b9ea4b91-3c4d-cf08-540b-576fc3c945db','957753b4-b0bf-e3a7-4e38-738968241d09','curriculum-v1-cp01','Understanding the Modern Technology Workplace','lesson','Understand the concept
Technology work combines technical execution with communication, judgment and collaboration. Read role descriptions as collections of responsibilities rather than lists of fashionable tools. Distinguish required capabilities from preferences and identify artifacts that could demonstrate each one. Avoid claiming readiness solely from course completion.

Apply it to a concrete case
A junior role asks for API work and teamwork. A small tested API plus a clear review discussion demonstrates more than a list of tools in a profile. State the scope of your own contribution.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Listing a tool on a CV proves the ability to use it professionally. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('4b6e768b-6df0-572e-82ec-8921b72594fa','957753b4-b0bf-e3a7-4e38-738968241d09','curriculum-v1-cp02','Communication','lesson','Understand the concept
Professional communication helps a reader decide or act. Lead with the relevant outcome, provide supporting evidence and state the requested action or next step. Separate observed facts from assumptions and explain uncertainty precisely. Adapt detail to the audience without hiding a material limitation.

Apply it to a concrete case
Instead of saying the feature is done, report that creation and reload tests passed, cross-user testing remains open and a reviewer is needed before release. This gives the team a usable decision point.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A confident status message is more useful than an accurate qualified one. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('355a4e7a-8b51-2b28-1c7d-b4458b4a63a3','957753b4-b0bf-e3a7-4e38-738968241d09','curriculum-v1-cp03','Collaboration & Teamwork','lesson','Understand the concept
Collaboration needs shared goals and clear boundaries between contributions. Agree on ownership, interface contracts and review expectations before parallel work. Raise conflicts early and resolve them using the project requirements and evidence. Credit others accurately and make handoffs reproducible rather than dependent on private context.

Apply it to a concrete case
One teammate changes an API response while another builds its UI. Agree on a response contract and notify the consumer before changing it; then test the integrated behavior together.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Dividing tasks removes the need to coordinate interfaces. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('821a8fe1-6450-2693-fdb1-3e1c13f5c661','957753b4-b0bf-e3a7-4e38-738968241d09','curriculum-v1-cp04','Critical Thinking & Problem Solving','lesson','Understand the concept
Problem solving begins by stating the observed behavior and the expected behavior. Generate plausible explanations, identify evidence that would distinguish them and test the smallest useful hypothesis. Avoid changing many variables at once. Record what the evidence supports and revise the explanation when observations contradict it.

Apply it to a concrete case
A dashboard total is wrong. Check source records, query aggregation and display formatting separately instead of changing all three. A duplicated join explains the count and predicts which cases should fail.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: The first plausible explanation is the root cause. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('b414c36a-e0fc-ee5d-d4d9-a7c17c5bd6aa','caa32e0d-88be-310b-6be5-6da90fdbb192','curriculum-v1-cp05','Building a Technical Portfolio','lesson','Understand the concept
A portfolio should let a reader inspect what you did and how it was checked. Include the problem, your contribution, artifacts, test evidence and limitations. Distinguish a personal exercise from deployed work and a claimed skill from independently reviewed evidence. Share only material you are authorized to make visible.

Apply it to a concrete case
A team project entry names the API endpoint you implemented and links its tests, while crediting the UI work to a teammate. Private user data is excluded from screenshots and repository examples.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A team project can be presented as entirely your own work. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('f7aa9f4b-927d-2da8-193c-c66239578465','caa32e0d-88be-310b-6be5-6da90fdbb192','curriculum-v1-cp06','CV, LinkedIn & Professional Presence','lesson','Understand the concept
Professional profiles summarize evidence relevant to a role. Use specific contributions and documented outcomes, keeping claims proportionate to what was actually measured. Do not invent employers, credentials, users or performance improvements. Keep public details consistent and link to permitted artifacts that substantiate important claims.

Apply it to a concrete case
Built a tested task API is supportable with code and tests. Increased productivity by 80 percent is not supportable without a defined measurement and evidence. Use the first claim until the second is established.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Plausible impact numbers are acceptable when they make a CV stronger. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('3be8604a-6e4f-d646-da61-feccbc8ca723','caa32e0d-88be-310b-6be5-6da90fdbb192','curriculum-v1-cp07','Interviews & Demonstrating Competence','lesson','Understand the concept
An interview answer should connect a problem, your action, the reasoning and the observed result. Use artifacts or examples when possible and distinguish your contribution from the team effort. When you do not know an answer, explain how you would investigate rather than inventing certainty. Practice receiving feedback and improving clarity.

Apply it to a concrete case
Asked about a bug, explain the failing case, the duplicated join you found, the test you added and the corrected result. Do not claim ownership of unrelated parts of the system.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Admitting an unknown is always worse than offering a confident guess. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('13175530-c422-d4b7-c5fe-09ba3792eb10','caa32e0d-88be-310b-6be5-6da90fdbb192','curriculum-v1-cp08','Career Readiness Project','lab','Understand the concept
Career readiness is a set of demonstrated capabilities and remaining gaps, not an unsupported employability score. Select a target role, map its requirements to permitted artifacts and identify missing evidence. Produce consistent application materials and a realistic next-learning plan. Keep verification states visible so reviewers can distinguish practice from approved work.

Apply it to a concrete case
A learner has a tested API but no deployment evidence. The portfolio presents the API honestly and the next plan includes a supervised deployment exercise rather than claiming production experience.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Completing a career course guarantees employment readiness for every role. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('8f332195-1f06-4576-6fda-5a54dacc594f','f0be474e-f02c-f8d8-76e5-d59bfa597085','curriculum-v1-ei01','Problems Worth Solving','lesson','Understand the concept
A product idea should start with a specific person, situation and recurring difficulty. Separate direct observations from assumptions about causes or willingness to pay. Consider the workaround already used and the cost of doing nothing. A problem statement should remain meaningful even if the first proposed technology is removed.

Apply it to a concrete case
Students coordinate study rooms through repeated messages and sometimes arrive to find no space. The problem is unreliable coordination, not the absence of an AI app. Investigate the current process first.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A novel technology automatically identifies a worthwhile customer problem. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('6269c53d-541c-207d-d1cc-8afba57c1bc3','f0be474e-f02c-f8d8-76e5-d59bfa597085','curriculum-v1-ei02','Customer Discovery','lesson','Understand the concept
Discovery interviews seek evidence about existing behavior, constraints and priorities. Ask open questions about recent experiences rather than asking whether someone likes your proposed solution. Obtain appropriate consent, minimize personal data and distinguish quotations from interpretations. A small interview sample provides leads and uncertainty, not proof of a whole market.

Apply it to a concrete case
Would you use my smart booking app invites politeness. Tell me about the last time you tried to find a study room reveals actions, obstacles and alternatives without suggesting the answer.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Positive reactions to a pitch prove demand. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('923d06df-1a4b-d8a6-3447-65ba1b6d6d6c','f0be474e-f02c-f8d8-76e5-d59bfa597085','curriculum-v1-ei03','Evaluating Ideas','lesson','Understand the concept
Evaluate an idea by the importance of the problem, who experiences it, existing alternatives and the hardest assumptions. Separate evidence from confidence and choose a low-cost test of the riskiest claim. Feasibility, desirability and sustainability are different questions. A scoring table helps organize judgment but does not turn guesses into facts.

Apply it to a concrete case
A room-booking idea assumes staff will maintain availability data. Before building a polished app, test whether a small group can keep a shared availability record accurate for a week.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A high score in an idea matrix proves the business will succeed. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('745c3660-62ca-e6b7-a13c-45ceb667bd37','f0be474e-f02c-f8d8-76e5-d59bfa597085','curriculum-v1-ei04','Value Proposition','lesson','Understand the concept
A value proposition connects a specific user problem to a benefit the user can recognize. Explain the alternative currently used and why the proposed change could be better. Avoid vague claims such as smarter or revolutionary. Define a measurable outcome and test whether users value it enough to change behavior.

Apply it to a concrete case
Find an available room without messaging five groups is more concrete than AI-powered campus innovation. Test whether the proposed process actually reduces unsuccessful searches.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A list of product features is the same as a user value proposition. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('3b102466-3622-4e86-0fcf-fc49ab7d0215','76d42a14-c7b6-d3f9-2405-b0db85321001','curriculum-v1-ei05','Business Models','lesson','Understand the concept
A business model describes how value is delivered and sustained. Identify the user, payer, distribution route and recurring costs, which may be different from initial build costs. Use explicit assumptions and simple calculations before projecting growth. Do not present fictional revenue or demand as measured results.

Apply it to a concrete case
A service earns a fictional 100 units per month but costs 120 units to operate. More users may worsen the loss if costs scale faster than revenue. Separate fixed and per-user costs before extrapolating.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Growing user numbers always improve financial sustainability. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('cfac1136-32a0-fc11-463b-d65f8b551191','76d42a14-c7b6-d3f9-2405-b0db85321001','curriculum-v1-ei06','Building an MVP','lesson','Understand the concept
A minimum viable product is a bounded way to learn about a value proposition, not a license to ignore safety or quality. Select the assumption to test and include only the capabilities needed for that test. Define a success threshold, protect participant data and state what the prototype cannot do. A manual service may test demand before software is necessary.

Apply it to a concrete case
Before building automated room matching, manually coordinate a small authorized group using a shared schedule. Measure successful bookings and effort to learn whether coordination solves the problem.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An MVP must contain every major feature of the eventual product. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('7213aabc-33bf-d283-0b8c-4246f3f0da29','76d42a14-c7b6-d3f9-2405-b0db85321001','curriculum-v1-ei07','Testing, Feedback & Iteration','lesson','Understand the concept
An experiment needs a question, procedure and decision rule. Observe actual behavior and record negative feedback as well as positive reactions. Compare results with the original threshold instead of redefining success afterward. Choose the next change based on the evidence and preserve a record of what was learned.

Apply it to a concrete case
A booking prototype gets compliments but only one of ten participants completes a booking. Investigate the failed steps and value assumption rather than counting compliments as adoption.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Positive feedback is equivalent to demonstrated adoption. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('0f928121-7f90-be65-c21d-1ccb2572b39e','76d42a14-c7b6-d3f9-2405-b0db85321001','curriculum-v1-ei08','Startup/MVP Project','lab','Understand the concept
A startup project should show the problem, discovery evidence, risky assumptions, experiment and result. Keep participant information protected and clearly label simulated evidence. Explain what changed after feedback and what remains unknown. The final recommendation may be to stop or change direction; that can be a sound outcome when supported by evidence.

Apply it to a concrete case
Interviews reveal that room availability data is unreliable, and a manual trial shows maintaining it is costly. The team narrows the service to one managed venue instead of claiming campus-wide readiness.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A project is unsuccessful if evidence suggests abandoning the original idea. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('d313d1b1-f72e-7f8d-4330-b491adbe2bd7','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc01','What Is Vibe Coding?','lesson','Understand the concept
AI-assisted development uses a coding assistant to propose or implement software changes. The developer remains responsible for requirements, architecture, access boundaries and the observed behavior of the result. Start with a small task, inspect the proposed code and compare it with acceptance criteria. A generated explanation or completion claim is not execution evidence. Preserve a manual path when the assistant is unavailable and disclose assistance honestly.

Apply it to a concrete case
An agent implements a task counter and says tests pass, but provides no run output. Inspect the diff, execute a test with zero and multiple tasks and record the actual result. If the counter includes deleted tasks, reject the completion claim and investigate the query.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A coding agent completion message is sufficient evidence that the feature works. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,1) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('c663faaf-0f73-15bc-9973-475c109c8105','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc02','Idea → Build Specification','lesson','Understand the concept
A build specification states the user, desired outcome, inputs, observable behavior and exclusions. Include unhappy paths and data ownership rather than describing only a screen. Separate required behavior from optional polish and identify unresolved decisions before coding. The specification should let a reviewer decide whether a change meets the need without guessing what the author intended.

Apply it to a concrete case
For a study-task organizer, require an owner-scoped task list, nonempty titles and persistence after reload. Exclude shared tasks from the first version. Acceptance includes rejecting another user update and showing a failed-save message without losing input.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A screenshot or one-sentence idea fully specifies application behavior. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,2) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('9b850380-2c13-7777-d850-4b3199f7df74','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc03','Prompting Coding Agents','lesson','Understand the concept
An agent brief should identify the outcome, constraints, repository entry points and tests that demonstrate success. Ask the agent to inspect existing code before choosing changes and to preserve established architecture unless the task requires otherwise. Specify stop conditions for missing information or unsafe effects. Require a diff summary and actual validation results, keeping secrets out of prompts and logs.

Apply it to a concrete case
A request to fix task validation names the current form, server command and database constraint. It asks for the smallest change and tests for empty and whitespace-only titles. It does not authorize replacing authentication or deploying the app.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Broad permission to improve the codebase is the best default for a small defect. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,3) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('364b9e64-e2b5-4354-1b7c-b2b0508fab80','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc04','Understanding Existing Codebases','lesson','Understand the concept
Read repository instructions, package scripts, recent history and the files reached by the feature. Trace UI events through actions or handlers, services, database operations and tests. Distinguish active runtime code from examples or unused files. Record existing behavior and run relevant checks before editing so pre-existing failures are not confused with regressions.

Apply it to a concrete case
A page calls a server action that invokes a database command. A similarly named client helper is unused. Change the active command path and verify its RLS behavior instead of fixing only the unused helper.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A filename or architecture document proves a feature is wired into production. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,4) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('15133c4e-0558-d8a7-f9c8-0854d0dfeb45','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc05','Build Your First AI-Assisted Application','lesson','Understand the concept
A vertical slice connects one useful user action from interface to persistent result. Start with a minimal task and add validation, error feedback and a reproducible check before expanding. Review every generated dependency and code change for necessity. Keep progress in small commits and distinguish a local prototype from a deployed service.

Apply it to a concrete case
Build task creation first: enter a title, validate it, save the record and reload the list. Test an empty title and a failed save. Only after this slice works should filters or visual refinements be added.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Generating all screens first is proof that the underlying application is complete. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,5) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5a1d2cae-3b70-bbaa-8a73-7ba207136f37','36fbeea6-3da5-83b0-4431-ce3296267151','curriculum-v1-vc06','AI-Assisted Frontend Development','lesson','Understand the concept
Use an assistant to propose UI changes within the existing component and style system. Inspect semantics, labels, keyboard operation and responsive behavior as well as appearance. Separate local form state from confirmed server state. Preserve user input after recoverable errors and prevent duplicate submissions while a request is pending without permanently disabling recovery.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task form looks correct but its submit control is a clickable div. Replace it with a semantic button, associate the label with the input and test keyboard submission. On failed save, retain the title and show an actionable error.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Visual similarity to a mockup is sufficient frontend verification. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,6) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('af829403-4be3-9e09-7d75-4ca08678decb','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc07','Backend, Database & APIs','lesson','Understand the concept
Backend changes must validate untrusted input and derive identity from the authenticated session. Use canonical service boundaries and database constraints rather than inventing a parallel write path. Prefer additive migrations, inspect row-level policies and verify cross-user denial. Keep secrets server-side and define request, response and error contracts so the UI can recover correctly.

Apply it to a concrete case
Adding due dates requires a nullable column for existing tasks, input validation for new values and unchanged owner-scoped updates. A generated policy allowing every authenticated user to update all tasks must be rejected.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: An authenticated database role should be allowed to update every application record. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,7) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('7020cf45-73a2-a737-010c-a7ee54c9308f','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc08','Debugging With AI','lesson','Understand the concept
Give the assistant the expected behavior, actual behavior, minimal reproduction and relevant safe logs. Form hypotheses and inspect the responsible state before editing. Change the smallest causal element and add a regression test that would fail on the original defect. Avoid repeated speculative rewrites, and remove temporary diagnostics that expose unnecessary information.

Apply it to a concrete case
A task count doubles only when a task has two comments. The reproduction suggests a join multiplication problem. Count distinct tasks or change the query structure, then verify zero, one and multiple-comment cases.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Repeatedly asking an agent to try another patch is equivalent to diagnosing the cause. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,8) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('5f535b96-ad34-0ab6-b98c-f3a23988654f','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc09','Git/GitHub for AI Development','lesson','Understand the concept
Inspect repository status before work, keep unrelated changes intact and use a focused branch for a bounded task. Read the diff before staging, checking for accidental files, secrets and scope expansion. Commit coherent changes with the problem and validation evidence. A pull request should explain behavior and limitations to someone who did not see the agent conversation.

Apply it to a concrete case
An agent fixes a label but also reformats the entire repository. Retain the necessary label change and avoid bundling unrelated churn. Review the final diff and run the relevant check before creating a focused commit.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: Every file changed by an agent belongs in the task commit. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,9) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('33c73104-412d-763c-027e-6c7f56a43428','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc10','Testing & E2E Verification','lesson','Understand the concept
Unit tests check focused logic, integration tests check boundaries and browser tests check a user journey. Use assertions that would catch the defect or missing behavior, not just mirror implementation details. Verify persistence after reload and exercise invalid input, interrupted requests and unauthorized access. Never replace production logic with a test-only shortcut to obtain a green result.

Apply it to a concrete case
A browser test creates a task and sees it in memory, but never reloads. Add a reload and verify the saved task through the real backend, then test that a second user cannot edit it. Record skipped tests as unverified.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A passing mocked UI test proves the production persistence path works. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,10) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('4a10c8e4-874f-da18-ced5-846f1c5bb1ed','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc11','Security & Responsible Vibe Coding','lesson','Understand the concept
Generated code can introduce excessive privileges, unsafe input handling or accidental secret exposure. Inspect the diff at trust boundaries and test authorization outside the UI. Use only authorized test accounts and synthetic data, avoid posting credentials to an assistant and rotate any credential that was exposed. Human responsibility includes understanding why a mitigation works and reporting residual risk.

Apply it to a concrete case
A generated client component embeds an administrative key to bypass a failed query. Remove the privileged client path, rotate any exposed key and repair the authorized server/database path. Passing the query is not worth removing the access boundary.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A workaround that makes the feature pass is acceptable even if it bypasses authorization. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,45,11) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
insert into public.learning_activities(id,module_id,slug,title,kind,body,requires_output,estimated_minutes,sort_order) values ('940148ad-cdfe-4c17-da3b-dc15730cdcc0','f46fcd8a-35c0-ac48-aa02-4abf36ab373b','curriculum-v1-vc12','Production Application Capstone','lab','Understand the concept
The capstone joins requirements, architecture, implementation and operations into one reviewable delivery. Keep agent work bounded and record your own technical decisions. Demonstrate a working UI and backend/data path where applicable, focused Git history, unit/integration/browser tests, security checks and an actual authorized deployment. Include health observations, recovery instructions, a README and reflection on errors caught. Unexecuted checks or an undeployed prototype cannot be described as a production release.

Apply it to a concrete case
A study-task application is deployed to a test environment, tested through creation and reload, and checked with two users for isolation. A release report links the exact commit, test outputs, deployment, README and rollback procedure. An unresolved security failure blocks approval even if the UI works.

Inspect the result
Use the method above on the practice task. Record the input, your decision, its supporting reason and the actual result of a check. Explain how your result avoids this mistake: A production-oriented capstone can claim deployment or security verification without executing those checks. A plan or generated claim is not evidence that a check ran.',true,180,12) on conflict (module_id,slug) do nothing;
